meta {
  name: Delete category
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/categories/{{categoryId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  TICKET-P6-003 — deletes the category. Ratings filed under it are NOT deleted and are not touched by
  the controller at all: `Rating.categoryId`'s `onDelete: SetNull` does the work at the database layer,
  so they simply become uncategorised.

  Response:
  - 204, empty body.
  - 400 `{ code: 'invalid_category_id' }` — `:id` is not a UUID.
  - 403 `{ error: 'category_forbidden', message }` — the category belongs to another user.
  - 404 `{ error: 'category_not_found', message }` — no category with that id.
}
